-- The 71 items of Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood - symbiotes, magic slimes,
-- shock parasites, blood stones and magic crystals. 10 vehicle, 60 magic, 1 armor.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-wormwood-gear.sql
--
-- Transcribed from the OCR cache (.cache/books/ww, 300dpi, no text layer) and
-- reconciled against the book's OWN list of symbiotic organisms, parasites,
-- blood stones and magic crystals on printed page 91 - the one page that names
-- every item in the book in a single place.
--
-- THAT LIST EARNED ITS KEEP. The Spell Gem of Magic's description heading falls
-- on the printed 113/114 page break and does not survive it, so reading the
-- description pages alone finds FOUR spell gems where the list names five. The
-- p.91 list is also what settles Half Mask: the Quick Find Table on printed 6
-- prints "Crawler: Half Mast", and the p.91 list and the p.97 heading both say
-- Half Mask. Two readings against one.
--
-- NOTHING HERE HAS A PRICE, and that is the book rather than a failed read.
-- Wormwood runs on barter - the Priest of Light O.C.C. states "Money: Not
-- applicable" outright (p.54) - and every one of these items is grown by the
-- living planet or summoned by a prayer, not sold. So cost stays NULL and
-- cost_note records why, rather than an invented figure or the estimate marker,
-- which would claim a price was looked for and not found.
--
-- NAMES TAKE THEIR GROUP AS A PREFIX where the bare name is meaningless in a
-- picker. The p.91 list prints "Crown", "Necklace", "Spider" and "Half Mask";
-- the book's own Quick Find Table indexes them as "Crawler: Crown" and so on,
-- and that is the form used here, matching the catalog's existing sub-skill
-- convention. The claws and stars follow the same rule. The worms already name
-- themselves and are left alone.
--
-- CATEGORIES. The battle saint, its orb and all eight parasites are 'vehicle':
-- the book calls the battle saint a land vehicle and pilots it like a giant
-- robot, the krikton battle wagon carries a rider and three passengers, and the
-- catalog already files a Riding Horse there. Worms of Armor are 'armor' - they
-- ARE mega-damage body armour, 60 M.D.C. at 20 lbs. Everything else is 'magic'.
--
-- ONE SLUG COLLISION, deliberately renamed. The catalog already holds
-- 'crystal-ball' from the Palladium Fantasy magic item list. Wormwood's is a
-- different object - grown from the ground, 110 M.D.C., useless outside its
-- claw pedestal - so it is 'wormwood-crystal-ball', named Wormwood Crystal
-- Ball. Nothing else in these 71 collides with the 902 rows already live.
--
-- THE SPELLS LISTED INSIDE THESE ITEMS ARE CROSS-REFERENCES, not new rows.
-- Armor of Ithan, Eyes of Thoth, Mystic Portal, Call Lightning and the rest are
-- existing Rifts invocations the gems cast; the prayers under the Eye and Heart
-- of Wormwood are the 37 added by add-wormwood-prayers.sql. Nothing in this
-- file inserts a spell.
--
-- ON CONFLICT (slug) DO UPDATE rather than INSERT OR IGNORE, so this file is
-- the authoritative bytes in every environment. Pure ASCII with LF endings.

INSERT INTO gear
  (slug, name, system, category, weight_lbs, cost, cost_note, damage, is_mega_damage, range, payload, rate_of_fire, ar, sdc, mdc, description, source_book)
VALUES
  ('battle-saint', 'Battle Saint', 'rifts', 'vehicle', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', 'Restrained punch 1D6 M.D., full punch or kick 1D6x10 M.D., power punch 2D6x10 M.D., judo body throw 5D6x10 M.D. Double damage to supernatural monsters and creatures of magic.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A giant, organic combat robot grown by the living planet - one of only twelve known to exist. It requires one HUMAN pilot who physically joins to the creature; human-like beings cannot operate one, though up to 24 can ride inside the hollow octagonal head. M.D.C. is the pilot''s own hit points or M.D.C. times 20, so a pilot with 32 instills 640. Head is half the main body, arms and legs 25% each, hands 10% each. Height 100 to 200 feet (30.5 to 61 m), width 25 feet (7.6 m), weight 2D4x10,000 tons, speed 3D6x10, leap 100 feet, supernatural P.S. 60. A land vehicle; it cannot fly. Attacks per melee equal the pilot''s plus three. Does not fatigue; impervious to poisons, drugs, gases, normal fire, cold, S.D.C. weapons, possession, mind control and illusions, but M.D. weapons, energy attacks and magic do full damage. Four times per 24 hours it can use Call Lightning, Heat Point, Hell Fire, Invisibility, Levitate, Breathe Without Air and Close Rift, each at 12th level. It has a 24-hour fuel capacity and then needs a full 24 hours of rest. Only the apok, knights of the Temple or Hospital, and monks can pilot one; a priest of light can summon but not pilot. Off-worlders need to be a major or master psionic, cyber-knight or True Atlantean. The Forces of Darkness cannot summon, use or corrupt one.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.93-94'),
  ('battle-saint-orb', 'Battle Saint Orb', 'rifts', 'vehicle', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', 'Restrained ram 2D6 M.D., full strength ram 1D6x10 M.D. Double damage to supernatural monsters and creatures of magic.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The flying counterpart of the battle saint, and despite the name an octagonal shape rather than a sphere. M.D.C. is the pilot''s own hit points or M.D.C. times 10. Height and width 12 to 20 feet (3.6 to 6 m), weight 1D4x10 tons, speed 4D4x10 flying to a maximum altitude of 5000 feet (1534 m). No supernatural P.S. and no leap. Does not fatigue; impervious to poisons, drugs, gases, normal fire, cold, S.D.C. weapons, possession, mind control and illusions, but M.D. weapons, energy attacks and magic do full damage. Five times per 24 hours it can use Breathe Without Air, Create Opening, Call Lightning, Dispel Magic Barriers, Energy Disruption, Fire Ball, Heat Point, Hell Fire, Invisibility, Negate Magic, Protection Circle: Simple and Tongues, each at 7th level. The Forces of Darkness cannot summon, use or corrupt one.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.94-95'),
  ('spirit-of-wormwood', 'Spirit of Wormwood', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A shimmering white ectoplasmic mist in a vaguely humanoid shape with wispy energy wings, which peasants call an angel. It attaches to a WILLING host of good alignment only (principled, scrupulous or unprincipled) and cannot then be removed, dispelled or disguised - it simply disappears after 3D4 hours. Powers, all psionic ones at 6th level: fly at 50 mph (80 km) to 2000 feet (610 m); semi-impervious to energy including magic energy (half damage); an energy field worth an extra 40 M.D.C.; +3 to save vs horror factor; Sense Evil, Sense Magic, Sixth Sense, Presence Sense and Clairvoyance; and imperviousness to other symbiotes, possession and mind control. Its greatest power is intuitive knowledge of Wormwood: the wearer knows the exact location and heading of crawling towers and the location of demon cities, armies, the Host and the Unholy within 200 miles (320 km). Only one can be worn at a time. It cannot be used or altered by the Forces of Darkness.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.95-96'),
  ('claw-booster', 'Claw: Booster', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 40, 'Attached to the face around one of the character''s eyes; the evil Salome wears one. Powers: lets the host see the invisible (the eye around the claw turns solid red or black), increases M.D.C./hit points, P.P.E. and I.S.P. by 50%, and increases spell strength by one level. Penalties: reduce P.B. by 20% and all skills by -10%, as the character comes to rely on magic and natural abilities rather than skills and equipment; the character becomes cocky and arrogant, and evil or selfish ones may become power hungry. Like all claws it has 40 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 1D4x10 points every melee at the cost of one of its host''s P.P.E., and dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.96'),
  ('claw-combat', 'Claw: Combat', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', '+1D6 M.D. on that hand, plus damage from supernatural P.S.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 40, 'Placed on top of the character''s hand and fingers, where it adheres. Powers: gives that hand and arm supernatural strength, inflicts an additional 1D6 M.D. plus supernatural P.S. damage, and grants one additional attack per melee round. Penalties: reduce P.B. by one point and skill performance by -5%, because the character loves fighting and has difficulty concentrating on anything else. Only one claw can be worn per pair of hands. 40 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 1D4x10 per melee at the cost of one host P.P.E., dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.96'),
  ('claw-feet', 'Claw: Feet', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', '+1D6 M.D. from kicks.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 40, 'A pair attached to the tops of the feet, similar in application to the combat claw. Powers: increases running speed by 25%, adds six feet (1.8 m) to leaps, +10% to climb and balance skills, and inflicts an additional 1D6 M.D. from kicks. Penalties: reduce P.P. by one point and skill performance by -5%; the character comes to prefer open spaces and wilderness and dislikes confining buildings and crowded cities. 40 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 1D4x10 per melee, dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.96'),
  ('claw-eye', 'Claw: Eye', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 40, 'A flat circular body the size of a silver dollar with three tentacle-like stalks, each ending in a claw holding an eyeball. Each stalk extends about a foot and moves independently, so each eye can look in a different direction; everything the symbiote sees, its host sees. Usually attached to the middle of the forehead or the base of the neck. Powers: see the invisible, see aura (as the psionic power), keen color vision, sight in three directions at once, +2 on initiative, and it cannot be surprised by sneak or back attacks. Penalties: reduce P.B. by 25%; the character has trouble sleeping (never more than six hours) and tends to be jumpy and on edge. 40 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 1D4x10 per melee, dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.96'),
  ('crawler-brain-sucker', 'Crawler: Brain Sucker', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 50, 'Attaches to the top of the head and resembles a salamander with six tentacles instead of legs, a thick flat body ending in a tail, and a pair of tiny eyes. Powers: the wearer is completely impervious to psionic attack, magic illusions and mind control of all kinds, and gains see the invisible and nightvision to 100 feet (30.5 m). Penalties: reduce I.Q. by 25% and the performance of all skills by -25%. Like all crawlers it has 50 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 1D4x10 points every melee at the cost of one of its host''s P.P.E., and dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.96'),
  ('crawler-chest-wrap', 'Crawler: Chest Wrap', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 50, 'An insect with a long body, head, eyes, antennae and six long legs. The body rests in the centre of the chest, the two front legs reaching up around the neck or shoulders and the remaining four wrapping the rib cage. The evil Salome wears one. Powers: an additional 80 M.D.C., repaired at 10 points an hour, and resistance to fire and heat - though magic fire and plasma weapons inflict full damage. Penalties: reduces P.B. and M.A. by one point each. 50 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 1D4x10 per melee, dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.96-97'),
  ('crawler-crown', 'Crawler: Crown', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 50, 'Looks like a strange plant, yellow to green to turquoise, with a dozen or two long stem-like tentacles standing straight up and six thicker ones used as legs. Attaches to the top of the head and is worn like a headdress or crown of spikes. Powers: impervious to fire and heat (even magic fire and plasma weapons do only half damage), impervious to disease and to magic sicknesses including curses, nightvision to 1000 feet (305 m), resistance to poison and drugs (+2 to save, and the drug is only half as potent), and bio-regeneration of 2D6 M.D.C./hit points per melee round. Penalties: reduces the character''s P.P.E. base by one third. 50 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 1D4x10 per melee, dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.97'),
  ('crawler-half-mask', 'Crawler: Half Mask', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 50, 'One of the few crawlers that does not resemble an animal - a half-moon fragment of metal plate or shell that crawls on a hundred tiny legs until it adheres to the side of a face and encircles one eye, the legs burrowing into the flesh. That eye then looks like an eyeball in a skull. Powers: increases M.D.C./hit points by 50% and creates a permanent, constant mind block so powerful that psychics cannot see the aura or sense anything at all about the wearer; the character is also impervious to empathic and telepathic communication and attacks, hypnotic suggestion and illusions. Penalties: reduce P.B. by 25%. The character is closed to HELPFUL psionics too, and any psychic sensitive powers they had are obliterated while the mask is worn. The face stays horribly scarred even after a priest removes it, so the P.B. penalty is permanent. 50 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 1D4x10 per melee, dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.97'),
  ('crawler-medallion-heart', 'Crawler: Medallion Heart', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 50, 'A heart-shaped beetle or crab-looking thing about the size of a softball, attached to the chest just over the heart. Powers: increases P.S. by five points, the character never fatigues, and +20% to save vs coma/death. Penalties: reduces speed by 20%. 50 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 1D4x10 per melee, dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.97'),
  ('crawler-medallion-skull', 'Crawler: Medallion Skull', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 50, 'A skull or death''s head shaped thing with three legs protruding from each side, attached to the chest, shoulder or back. Powers: the wearer is impervious to life or energy draining of any kind, including spell attacks, P.P.E. vampires, ordinary vampires, other symbiotes, life force batteries and life force cauldrons. Penalties: reduces M.A. by 20%. 50 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 1D4x10 per melee, dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.97'),
  ('crawler-necklace', 'Crawler: Necklace', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 50, 'At a glance an ornate gold necklace set with ruby stones; closer inspection finds legs and large red eyes. The centipede-like symbiote is metallic gold and armour-plated, and completely encircles the neck. Powers: the wearer understands and speaks all languages, is impervious to poisons and drugs and to the vampire''s bite and powers, and is +2 to save vs disease and magic potions. Penalties: the ability to taste food is reduced by 25% and the voice sounds hoarse. 50 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 1D4x10 per melee, dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.97'),
  ('crawler-spider', 'Crawler: Spider', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', 'The wearer''s bite secretes a burning poison for +1D6 damage.', 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 50, 'A small black orb the size of a quarter with six long thin legs, attached anywhere on the face or neck. Powers: the wearer is impervious to poisons and toxins of all kinds and +2 to save vs magic potions and slime, and their bite secretes a poison that burns victims for an additional 1D6 points of damage. Penalties: reduce P.B. by 20% and M.A. by one point. 50 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 1D4x10 per melee, dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.97'),
  ('star-glimmerstar', 'Star: Glimmerstar', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 30, 'A small, flat, flexible semi-transparent crystal-like starfish that fits in the palm and is worn on one or both hands. Powers: creates a glimmering wall of mystic light made of a hundred star-shaped sparkles, which repels animated dead, vampires, shadow beasts and all creatures that thrive in darkness, and doubles as a signal. The wearer can also see in bright light, is impervious to the Blinding Flash spell, and can harmlessly deflect laser beams as a parry - a successful roll means no damage. The lights can be created twice per melee round, each counting as one melee action. Penalties: darkness makes the character nervous and their vision in the dark is about half as good as normal. Like all stars it has 30 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 20 points every melee at the cost of one host P.P.E., and dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.97-98'),
  ('star-mindstar', 'Star: Mindstar', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 30, 'A blue or violet starfish the size of a human hand to twice that, attached to the top of the head. Powers: Empathy, Empathic Transmission, Telepathy, Mind Block and Ectoplasm, with I.S.P. equal to the character''s M.E. times five. Penalties: makes the host absentminded, -1 on initiative and -5% on all skills, and receptive to hypnotic suggestion at -2 to save. 30 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 20 per melee, dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.98'),
  ('star-magicstar', 'Star: Magicstar', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 30, 'A small silver starfish covered in crystal scales that sparkle like tiny diamonds, attached anywhere on the head, neck or spine. Only one can be worn. Powers: senses the location of P.P.E. crystals and stones, life force batteries and cauldrons, food caves, water fountains, dimensional rifts and places of mystic power within 100 miles, and senses the presence of the Unholy and his Host within one mile (1.6 km). It is also a P.P.E. receptacle holding a random 1D6x10 points, usable only by the host and available once every hour. Penalties: it draws that energy from the ambient energy of the Living Planet, from the slain, AND from other living creatures around it - so the character''s regular companions are ALWAYS 10% below their normal P.P.E., which can spell trouble for practitioners of magic. 30 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 20 per melee, dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.98'),
  ('worms-of-armor', 'Worms of Armor', 'rifts', 'armor', 20, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 60, 'Large, thick worms that coil snugly around the upper body, waist and parts of the arms and legs, and are surprisingly light at 20 lbs (9 kg). Powers: they serve as mega-damage body armour providing 60 M.D.C. of protection, regenerating 10 M.D.C. per melee round. When all their M.D.C. is destroyed the symbiotes fall off and are absorbed back into the Living Planet. Penalties: -10% to prowl, acrobatics and gymnastics, and -5% to climb. Note: a typical wormspeaker wears one of each worm symbiote on his body and mouth, a disgusting sight worth -50% P.B.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.98-99'),
  ('worms-of-blood', 'Worms of Blood', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 'Tiny, thin, red worms. Powers: swallowing three alive magically negates poison, stops internal bleeding and heals its cause. Placing three inside a cut or wound immediately stops bleeding and heals it ten times faster than normal - completely healed, with little scarring to wormspeakers, within 3D4 minutes. Penalties: none. Typically six or nine are found or summoned at a time. Small worms have 10 M.D.C., bio-regenerate 10 points every melee at the cost of one host P.P.E., and die within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.99'),
  ('worms-of-mending', 'Worms of Mending', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 'Tiny worms resembling one-inch pieces of white thread. Powers: when ten or more are poured into an open cut, gash or wound they seal, cleanse and heal it - bleeding stops in under a minute, pain is halved, decaying flesh and germs are destroyed so infection is impossible, and within 2D4 minutes the wound is completely closed with no scarring. Penalties: none. Typically twenty are found or summoned at a time. 10 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 10 per melee, dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.99'),
  ('worms-of-power', 'Worms of Power', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 30, 'A large grey worm attached to the tongue or the inside of the mouth. Powers: spell magic - Energy Bolt, Energy Field, Energy Disruption, Impervious to Energy and Negate Magic Barriers, each castable four times a day at fifth level. Penalties: reduce P.B. by one point. Large worms have 30 M.D.C., bio-regenerate 10 points every melee at the cost of one host P.P.E., and die within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.99'),
  ('worms-of-seeing', 'Worms of Seeing', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 30, 'A large, pulsating white worm attached to the tongue, inside the mouth or on the neck. Powers: spell magic - See Aura, Eyes of Thoth, Eyes of the Wolf, Locate (once a day) and Oracle (once a day), each at seventh level and castable four times a day unless noted. The character can also sense the approach of the Unholy, his Host and the presence of alien intelligences, but cannot pinpoint their time of arrival, direction, numbers or purpose. Bonus: +1 to save vs mind control and illusions. Penalties: reduce P.B. by one point. 30 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 10 per melee, dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.99'),
  ('worms-of-speech', 'Worms of Speech', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 30, 'One thick, flat, grey worm that attaches itself to the tongue and enables the character to understand and speak - though not read - all languages. Powers: perpetual spell magic available as often as needed - Tongues, Calling and Commune with Spirits. Penalties: reduce P.B. by one point. 30 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 10 per melee, dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.98-99'),
  ('worms-of-spirit', 'Worms of Spirit', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 30, 'A large, thin purple worm attached to the tongue or the inside of the mouth. Powers: spell magic - Turn Dead, Repel Animals, Constrain Being, Exorcism, Water to Wine and Remove Curse, each castable four times a day at fifth level. Penalties: reduce P.B. by one point. 30 M.D.C., bio-regenerates 10 per melee, dies within 1D6 hours if removed from Wormwood.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.99'),
  ('life-force-battery', 'Life Force Battery', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A creation of the Unholy, who calls them his soul batteries. A fleshy sack roughly the size of a human with three tentacles of four to five foot (1.2 to 1.5 m) reach, each attaching to a human or humanoid D-Bee host and draining P.P.E. and blood - never enough to kill, only enough to keep the victim docile. The stored energy is drawn on by the Unholy, the Host, dark priests and evil sorcerers to power war machines, work magic, control parasites and open rifts. P.S. 18, Spd 3D4, M.D.C. 1D4x10. Attached victims have half their normal melee actions, speed and bonuses, and keep those penalties after release. When a battery is slain it releases a wave of P.P.E. doing 2D6 M.D. to everything within 20 feet (6 m). The threat of being hooked to one keeps the civilian populace in check; most of those attached are heroes and freedom fighters.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.99-100'),
  ('life-force-cauldron', 'Life Force Cauldron', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 300, 'The soul vat, as the Unholy calls it. A circular pool six to ten feet (1.8 to 3 m) across and 10 to 20 feet (3 to 6 m) deep, grown from the living planet like a fountain, only the water is thick and foul. Living beings are bound, weighted and drowned in it; at the moment of death a character''s P.P.E. doubles and is absorbed and stored. 300 M.D.C., regenerating within one minute like the walls of the living buildings - only a priest or wormspeaker can destroy it. 300 P.P.E. to create, and it holds a maximum of 2000 P.P.E. taken from its victims. It is used to create magic slime, slime potions and ointments (50 or more P.P.E.), parasites (150), worm zombies (250), demon beast guards (250) and life force batteries (300), and to summon entities. Only an anarchist or evil character will consider making one, and Wormwood resists its creation anywhere the Forces of Evil do not dominate.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.99-100'),
  ('slime-potion', 'Slime Potion', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'One vial of magic slime, made only from a life force cauldron at a cost of 50 P.P.E. It tastes bad, and works on whoever drinks it as one 10th-level spell chosen by its creator: Breathe Without Air, Compulsion, Death Trance, Domination, Fear, Heal, Invisibility (simple), Mute, Negate Toxins, Reduce Self, Sickness, Sleep, Tongues, Trance or Words of Truth. Most are debilitating or controlling and are used on prisoners made to drink them; few instill beneficial powers.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.100'),
  ('slime-ointment', 'Slime Ointment', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A salve of magic slime applied to all or part of the body, made only from a life force cauldron at 50 P.P.E. each. The magic conjures just enough to cover the area needed. Each works as one 10th-level spell: Agony (part of the body), Befuddle (the temples), Blind (the eyes), Eyes of Thoth (the eyes), Eyes of the Wolf (the eyes), Fear (over the heart), Heal (the wound), Mask of Deceit (the face), Mute (the throat), Resist Fire (the body) or Stone to Flesh (the body).', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.100'),
  ('debilitation-slime', 'Debilitation Slime', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Enough slime to cover an entire human-size creature, at a cost of 90 P.P.E. The victim is sluggish and disoriented and has trouble concentrating: -25% on the performance of all skills. P.S., P.P., Spd and attacks per melee round are all reduced by half, and the character fatigues twice as fast as normal.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.100'),
  ('null-slime', 'Null Slime', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Enough slime to cover a character or item up to twice human size. Whatever it covers is impervious to all magic and, if magical itself, rendered powerless - a dark priest or dragon covered in null slime cannot cast prayers or spells or use any magical power, and a rune weapon, magic stone, talisman or amulet cannot inflict mega-damage, cast magic or provide bonuses. The slime is sticky and takes 3D4 melee rounds to remove; only a priest or wormspeaker can strip it instantly, using Remove Symbiotes.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.100'),
  ('restoration-slime', 'Restoration Slime', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Enough slime to cover an entire human-size creature, at a cost of 1000 P.P.E. - by far the most expensive slime the cauldron makes. It restores all lost hit points, S.D.C. and mega-damage, heals all wounds without scarring, and regenerates damaged organs and lost limbs within four hours.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.100'),
  ('stasis-slime', 'Stasis Slime', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Enough slime to cover an entire human-size creature, at a cost of 110 P.P.E. It slows the metabolism into a trance-like slumber, after which the character is dumped into a life force cauldron and rests unharmed and asleep at the bottom. Reviving means retrieving them and removing the slime; the revived person is in perfect health and full strength and only incredibly hungry. Food and perishables can be preserved the same way, for one decade per level of the cauldron maker. If the cauldron is destroyed, everything preserved in it magically appears and the slime oozes off, reviving them in seconds.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.100'),
  ('battler-parasite', 'Battler Parasite', 'rifts', 'vehicle', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', 'Restrained tap 1D6x10 S.D.C., restrained punch 1D6 M.D., full punch or claw swipe 6D6 M.D., power punch 2D4x10 M.D., tail strike 6D6 M.D., pinchers 4D6 M.D., bite 5D6 M.D., judo body throw 5D6 M.D., pounce 2D4x10 M.D.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 600, 'A giant monster that looks part dog and part insect, with an armour-plated head, four crystalline eyes, pinchers, a spiked prehensile tail used like a ball and chain, and articulated four-fingered claws. It can stand on its hind legs like a bear. M.D.C.: head 200, each eye 50, pinchers 40, hands 60 each, front legs 150 each, hind legs 200 each, tail 60, main body 600. Height 50 feet (15.2 m) on all fours and 90 to 100 feet (27.4 to 30.5 m) erect, 60 feet (18.3 m) long plus another 50 of tail, width 40 feet, weight 1200 to 2000 tons, speed 132 (90 mph/148 km), leap 200 feet (61 m), supernatural P.S. 50. Six attacks per melee. Bonuses: +2 initiative, +7 strike, +5 parry and dodge, +2 roll with impact, +6 to save vs the priest''s magic to repel, control and summon parasites. Horror Factor 18. I.Q. 2D4+4 and cunning, P.P. 22, P.B. 4; cannot fly. Does not fatigue, fearless, impervious to poisons, drugs, gases, normal fire, cold, possession, mind control, illusions and ordinary S.D.C. weapons; M.D. weapons, energy attacks, magic and psionics do full damage. Its pounce pins an opponent 20 feet or smaller 85% of the time. No magic or psionic powers. One rarely encounters more than one or two.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.101-102'),
  ('tick-parasite', 'Tick Parasite', 'rifts', 'vehicle', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', 'Restrained punch 5D6 S.D.C., full punch or claw swipe 3D6 M.D., power punch 6D6 M.D., pinchers 2D6 M.D., bite 4D6 M.D., pounce 2D4 M.D.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 60, 'A large oval body of lumpy flesh on six short thin legs, with a large mouth full of teeth and a pair of fangs. M.D.C.: head 50, each eye 10, pinchers 20, claws 10 each, legs 20 each, main body 60. Height four feet (1.2 m) on all fours and 7 to 8 feet (2.1 to 2.4 m) erect, 7 feet long, width four feet, weight 800 pounds (360 kg), speed 44 (30 mph/48 km), leap 20 feet (6 m), supernatural P.S. 28. Three attacks per melee. Bonuses: +1 initiative, +5 strike, +2 parry and dodge, +1 roll with impact. Horror Factor 9. P.P. 22, P.B. 2; cannot fly. Does not fatigue, fearless, impervious to poisons, drugs, gases, normal fire, cold, possession, mind control, illusions and ordinary S.D.C. weapons. Excellent climbers at 90/85% and can walk on any surface, walls and ceilings included, at full speed. Its pounce pins an opponent 10 feet or smaller 45% of the time. Typically travel in packs of 1D4+2.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.102'),
  ('beetle-parasite', 'Beetle Parasite', 'rifts', 'vehicle', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', 'Restrained punch 5D6 S.D.C., full punch or claw swipe 4D6 M.D., power punch 1D4x10 M.D., mandibles/pinchers 6D6 M.D., bite 4D6 M.D., pounce 2D4 M.D.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 90, 'The body of the tick with the head of the battler and larger pinchers, whose powerful mandibles can cut a man in half. M.D.C.: head 150, each eye 10, large pinchers 40, claws 20 each, legs 30 each, main body 90. Height five feet (1.5 m) on all fours and 12 to 15 feet (3.6 to 4.6 m) erect, 9 feet long, width five feet, weight 1200 pounds (540 kg), speed 44 (30 mph/48 km), leap 20 feet (6 m), supernatural P.S. 31. Three attacks per melee. Bonuses: +2 initiative, +4 strike, parry and dodge, +1 roll with impact. Horror Factor 13. P.P. 22, P.B. 2; cannot fly. Does not fatigue, fearless, impervious to poisons, drugs, gases, normal fire, cold, possession, mind control, illusions and ordinary S.D.C. weapons. Excellent climbers at 90/85% but cannot walk on walls and ceilings. Its pounce pins an opponent 10 feet or smaller 55% of the time. Typically hunts alone.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.102-103'),
  ('monster-worm-parasite', 'Monster Worm Parasite', 'rifts', 'vehicle', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', 'Full head butt or tail strike 4D6 M.D., power strike 1D4x10 M.D., pinchers 3D6 M.D., bite 6D6 M.D., lunge 1D6 M.D.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 150, 'A giant worm that snakes silently along the ground, its body long and slender with lumpy flesh, its maw huge and filled with teeth the length of short swords - large enough to swallow a man whole. It has two pairs of pinchers. M.D.C.: head 75, each eye 10, each pair of large pinchers 40, main body 150. Slithers rather than stands; the mouth opens five feet (1.5 m) wide. Length 15 to 30 feet (4.6 to 9 m), width four feet (1.2 m) in diameter, weight 2 to 8 tons, speed 27 (18.5 mph/29.7 km), supernatural P.S. 34. Three attacks per melee. Bonuses: +4 initiative, +4 strike, +2 parry and dodge. Horror Factor 15. P.P. 20, P.B. 1; cannot fly. Prowl 50%, swim 80%, track by smell 50%, track by blood scent 75%, bio-regenerates 2D6x10 M.D.C. every six hours. Does not fatigue, fearless, impervious to poisons, drugs, gases, normal fire, cold, possession, mind control, illusions and ordinary S.D.C. weapons. Fair climbers at 50/45% but cannot crawl on walls or ceilings. Its lunge knocks prey off its feet 40% of the time but it does not coil or crush. Typically hunts alone.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.103'),
  ('tangle-worm-parasite', 'Tangle Worm Parasite', 'rifts', 'vehicle', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', 'Full head butt or tail strike 3D6 M.D., tentacle strike 2D6 M.D., power strike 6D6 M.D., bite 3D6 M.D.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 100, 'A long worm-like body with an ugly turtle-like head full of teeth, and two long tentacles behind the head used to entangle, pin and drag prey to its jaws. M.D.C.: head 40, each eye 6, tentacles 40 each, main body 100. Body 12 to 20 feet (3.6 to 6 m) long with tentacles 15 to 20 feet (4.6 to 6 m), width two feet (0.6 m) in diameter, weight 800 to 1000 pounds (360 to 450 kg), speed 22 (15 mph/24 km), supernatural P.S. 26. Three attacks per melee. Bonuses: +2 initiative, +5 strike, parry and dodge. Horror Factor 14. P.P. 22, P.B. 1; cannot fly. Prowl 40%, swim 60%, track by smell 50%, track by blood scent 75%, bio-regenerates 1D6x10 M.D.C. every six hours. Does not fatigue, fearless, impervious to poisons, drugs, gases, normal fire, cold, possession, mind control, illusions and ordinary S.D.C. weapons. Good climbers at 70/65% but cannot crawl on walls or ceilings. Its entangle does no damage but pins an opponent 10 feet or smaller 50% of the time; even a failed entangle costs the target one melee action. Typically hunts in groups of 1D4+1.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.103-104'),
  ('krikton-flailer', 'Krikton Flailer', 'rifts', 'vehicle', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', 'Restrained punch 5D6 S.D.C., full punch or claw swipe 4D6 M.D., power punch 1D4x10 M.D., mandibles/pinchers 6D6 M.D., bite 4D6 M.D., tail whip 3D6 M.D., strangle or crush with tail 2D6 M.D. per attack, pounce 2D4 M.D.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 120, 'One of Lord Krikton''s parasitic monsters - roughly human-size, with a LOW HUMAN INTELLIGENCE that lets it use weapons and devices, though it still runs mostly on instinct and blood lust. Part worm and part insect: a shaggy head with four eyes and two pairs of mandibles, a long serpent-like body with a prehensile tail, four spindly insect legs and two long arms used to run and climb. M.D.C.: head 100, each eye 10, each pair of large pinchers 30, claws 20 each, arms 40 each, legs 50 each, tail section 60, main body 120. Height six feet (1.8 m) on all fours, 15 to 20 feet (4.6 to 6 m) long, 10 feet (3 m) erect resting on its tail like a cobra. Width four feet, weight 1200 pounds (540 kg), speed 33 (22.5 mph/36 km), leap 20 feet, supernatural P.S. 31. Five attacks per melee - four by punch, claw, weapon, bite or tail whip, plus one by entanglement. Bonuses: +2 initiative, +6 strike, +4 parry and dodge, +2 roll with impact, +3 to save vs magic, +4 to save vs the priest''s magic to repel, control and summon parasites. Horror Factor 15. I.Q. 2D4+2, P.P. 3D4+10, P.B. 2; cannot fly. Its pounce pins an opponent 10 feet or smaller 55% of the time and its tail entangles 35% of the time.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.104-105'),
  ('krikton-leaper', 'Krikton Leaper', 'rifts', 'vehicle', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', 'Restrained punch 6D6 S.D.C., full punch 5D6 M.D., power punch 1D6x10 M.D., kick 1D6x10 M.D., mandibles/pinchers 5D6 M.D., bite 4D6 M.D., head butt 2D6 M.D., stomp 2D6 M.D., pounce 2D4 M.D.', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 300, 'A demonic praying mantis four or five times the size and bulk of a human, with a huge armoured head, mandibles, four tiny eyes, thin but powerful arms and thick hind legs made for leaping. Its intelligence is below human but high for an animal: VERY OBEDIENT AND EASY TO TRAIN AND RIDE, and one or two sky riders or other demonic minions frequently ride on its back. M.D.C.: head 250, each eye 10, large pinchers 80, claws 40 each, arms 100 each, legs 250 each, main body 300. Height 12 feet (3.6 m) hunched, 20 feet (6 m) fully erect, nine feet crouched to leap. Width four or five feet, weight four to six tons, speed 58 (40 mph/64 km) running or an astonishing 110 (75 mph/120 km) leaping at full speed, leap 100 feet (30.5 m), supernatural P.S. 40. Five attacks per melee. Bonuses: +3 initiative, +6 strike, +5 parry and dodge, +2 roll with impact, +2 to save vs magic, +3 to save vs the priest''s magic to repel, control and summon parasites. Horror Factor 17. P.P. 3D4+10, P.B. 2; cannot fly. Prowl 25%, swim 50%, track by smell 60%, track by blood scent 75%, bio-regenerates 1D6x10 M.D.C. every hour. Good climbers at 70/65% but cannot walk on walls or ceilings. Its pounce knocks prey down 65% of the time and pins an opponent 10 feet or smaller 50% of the time.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.105-106'),
  ('krikton-battle-wagon', 'Krikton Battle Wagon', 'rifts', 'vehicle', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', 'Restrained punch 1D6x10 S.D.C., full punch 6D6 M.D., power punch 2D4x10 M.D., kick 1D6x10 M.D., bite 4D6 M.D., head butt 2D6 M.D., stomp 2D6 M.D., ram 4D6 M.D., spine throw 3D6 M.D. per spine.', 1, 'Spine throws: 500 feet (153 m).', 'Each of the four spine throwers holds 12 spines; the spines regenerate every hour.', 'One spine at a time or a volley of 2, 3 or 4 at the same target; a volley counts as one melee attack.', NULL, NULL, 500, 'The largest of the ridden parasites, and the one built to carry people: one rider sits behind the huge armoured head and as many as three more human-size passengers fit between its shoulders, with a techno-wizard weapon or energy gun frequently mounted on the head. It rolls on ball feet, retracting them and walking at half speed over rough terrain; it has only three legs, so it always moves in a loping up-and-down motion. Battle wagons used as riding animals are often painted or have their armoured hide etched with designs. M.D.C.: head 250, each eye 20, ball feet 100 each pair, legs 250 each, shoulder and rear armour plating 400, main body 500. Height 15 to 18 feet (4.6 to 5.5 m), 12 feet (3.6 m) long hunched, width ten feet (3 m), weight 20 to 25 tons, speed 44 (30 mph/48 km) running or an amazing 88 (60 mph/96 km) skating on its ball feet, leap 40 feet (12 m), supernatural P.S. 50. Four attacks per melee; each spine or volley counts as one melee action. Bonuses: +2 initiative, +6 strike, +2 parry, +4 dodge, +1 roll with impact, +5 to save vs magic, +2 to save vs the priest''s magic to repel, control and summon parasites. Horror Factor 17. P.P. 3D4+10, P.B. 2; cannot fly. Prowl 25%, swim 50%, track by smell 60%, track by blood scent 75%, bio-regenerates 1D6x10 M.D.C. every hour. Its ram knocks an opponent off its feet 65% of the time and counts as two melee actions.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.107-108'),
  ('battle-stone', 'Battle Stone', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A greater blood stone. A deep blood red, tear-shaped stone with a lighter red skull or death''s head in its centre. Powers: doubles the normal damage of any weapon it is built into and turns it into a magic weapon; set into body armour it doubles that armour''s M.D.C. Only one stone works per weapon or suit - multiple battle stones do NOT keep increasing damage or M.D.C. Duration: permanent as long as the stone is part of the item; it turns back into an ordinary weapon the moment the stone is removed.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.109'),
  ('bio-booster-stone', 'Bio-Booster Stone', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A greater blood stone. A burgundy oval with a permanent P.P.E. base of 60 points that practitioners of magic and priests cannot syphon. Powers: increases one of the character''s physical attributes by 50% - P.S. for 10 P.P.E., P.P. for 20, P.E. for 20, P.B. for 30, Spd for 10, or hit points/M.D.C. for 10. Each attribute booster is activated individually and each activation counts as one melee attack. Duration: one hour. The magical increase disappears the instant the character no longer has the stone.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.109-110'),
  ('bio-field-stone', 'Bio-Field Stone', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A greater blood stone. A crimson stone flecked with light red or orange stars, with a P.P.E. base of 60 that fully regenerates every 24 hours; when its energy is gone its powers cannot be used until it does. The character must touch or hold the stone, or the object it is set into, to evoke its protection. Powers: impervious to disease, radiation or airborne toxins (10 P.P.E.); impervious to fatigue for six hours (10); impervious to fire, heat and cold, though magic fire and plasma do full damage (10); impervious to poisons and drugs (10); protection from animals and insects, which leave the character alone unless a more alluring target is nearby (10); protection from parasites, which will not pester or attack the character but will assault those around him (15); and protection from evil spirits - impervious to possession of any kind and +2 to save vs mind control and magic illusions (30). Duration: one hour unless noted.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.110'),
  ('eye-stone', 'Eye Stone', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A greater blood stone, and the one with a permanent cost. A crimson stone the size and shape of a human eye with a darker red iris and pupil. One of the character''s organic eyes is REMOVED and the stone put in its place in the socket. Powers, all constant: nightvision to 1000 feet (305 m), see the invisible, see aura (as the psionic power), sight in the infrared spectrum, keen hawk-like colour vision, +5% to tracking, hunting, detect concealment, detect ambush, carpentry, picking locks, forgery and art, and +1 on initiative and +1 to parry and dodge. Penalties: reduce P.B. and M.E. by one point each; those attributes can only be restored by replacing the eye stone with an attractive cybernetic eye.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.110'),
  ('healing-stone', 'Healing Stone', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A greater blood stone. A deep, semi-opaque blood red stone in any of the smaller sizes, with a P.P.E. base of 60 that fully regenerates every 24 hours. The injured character must touch or hold it. Powers: heal wounds, restoring 4D6 hit points or M.D.C. with no scarring (10 P.P.E.); heal burns, soothing the pain and restoring 2D6 hit points with minimal scarring (10); negate poison, instantly cancelling poisons, toxins or drugs, purifying the blood and restoring 1D6 hit points (10); cure illness, halving the symptoms and penalties of disease, dispelling headaches and nausea, doubling recuperation and instantly negating magic illness though not curses (15); and stasis trance, a deep healing trance slowing respiration and heart rate almost to nothing, useful for slowing poison, conserving air or appearing dead, for up to four hours (5). Duration: instant effect.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.110'),
  ('psi-booster-stone', 'Psi-Booster Stone', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A greater blood stone. A crimson stone with a lighter starburst at its centre. Powers: increases the wearer''s I.S.P., psionic strength, range and duration by 50%, and their P.P.E., M.E. and M.A. by 25%. Duration: constant, as long as it is held or worn.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.110'),
  ('cat-s-eye-stone', 'Cat''s Eye Stone', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A lesser blood stone. Round like a marble, reddish orange with a narrow dark red strip through the middle that makes it resemble a cat''s eye. Power, pick ONE: nightvision to 200 feet (61 m), or see the invisible to 200 feet. Duration: constant, as long as it is held or worn.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.110'),
  ('mini-bio-booster-stone', 'Mini-Bio-Booster Stone', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A lesser blood stone - a tiny version of the greater bio-booster, with a permanent P.P.E. base of 30 that practitioners of magic and priests cannot syphon. Power: it increases exactly ONE physical attribute from the greater bio-booster stone''s list, picked once and never changed; how often it can be used depends on that power''s P.P.E. cost. Duration: one hour.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.110-111'),
  ('mini-healing-stone', 'Mini-Healing Stone', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A lesser blood stone - a tiny version of the greater healing stone, with a permanent P.P.E. base of 30 that cannot be syphoned. Power: it has exactly ONE of the greater healing stone''s powers, picked once and never changed; how often it can be used depends on that power''s P.P.E. cost. Duration: instant effect.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.111'),
  ('protection-stone', 'Protection Stone', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A lesser blood stone. Small, round, flat crimson disks with a permanent P.P.E. base of 30 that cannot be syphoned. Power: it has exactly ONE of the greater bio-field stone''s powers, picked once and never changed; how often it can be used depends on that power''s P.P.E. cost. Duration: one hour.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.111'),
  ('pure-stone', 'Pure Stone', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A lesser blood stone. A small teardrop of transparent red with a clear diamond-shaped centre. Power: purifies any water or drink it is placed into, and gives its user +1 to save vs poison and disease. Duration: instant effect; the bonus lasts as long as the stone is in the character''s possession.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.111'),
  ('spirit-stone', 'Spirit Stone', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A lesser blood stone. A small, round violet stone with a pink starburst at its centre. Power: the character is impervious to negative emotions transmitted by magic or psionics, including magic fear, despair and empathic transmission. Duration: constant, as long as it is held or worn.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.111'),
  ('control-gem', 'Control Gem', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A SUPER RARE greater crystal. It amplifies magic summoning and control, multiplying the duration of control, the range and the number of beings controlled by FIVE. It also grants eight spells per 24 hours in any combination or repetition, drawn from Calling, Constrain Being, Commune with Spirits, Control & Enslave Entity, Compulsion, Domination, Animate and Control Dead, Summon & Control Animals, Summon & Control Flies/Insects, Summon Entities, Summon Parasites and Trance. It also works like a crystal ball, though it can only observe the creatures it summoned or controls - and it can follow them through a rift into another dimension. Coveted by shifters, summoners and dark priests.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.111'),
  ('wormwood-crystal-ball', 'Wormwood Crystal Ball', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 110, 'An extremely rare greater crystal, and a different item from the Palladium Fantasy crystal ball. A completely smooth crystal orb the size of a soccer ball with 110 M.D.C., grown from the ground and held in a claw-like pedestal - the crystal must stay in its pedestal to function, and one without the other has no power. Powers: 20 P.P.E. activates it for 30 minutes and another 20 buys another 30. Once active it works like a satellite link camera, transmitting images from anywhere on Wormwood the observer is familiar with, switched between like television channels. It can see into other dimensions provided an active rift connects them and the observer has visited that dimension. There is no sound, only image. The view starts from a bird''s eye perspective and can zoom to a close-up, and the observer can follow a character into places he has never visited - but the moment he focuses on anything else he loses track of him. Others can watch, but only the activator controls the focus. Penalties: the observer loses track of time (30 minutes seems like five) and is so absorbed that he is easily caught off guard, at -4 on initiative. Replacing a lost or stolen crystal with a new one makes a working mechanism again.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.111'),
  ('greater-energy-cell-crystal', 'Greater Energy Cell Crystal', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A RARE greater crystal, usually pure white like a perfect diamond. It holds mystic energy that priests, practitioners of magic and techno-wizard devices can draw on, and regenerates half its P.P.E. in 12 hours and all of it in 24. Wormwood techno-wizards use these to power magic devices and to replace the fuel systems of energy weapons, motorcycles, hovercycles, machines and vehicles. Capacity by size: bowling ball 90 P.P.E., soccer ball 140 P.P.E., basketball 180 P.P.E.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.111-112'),
  ('life-essence-crystal', 'Life Essence Crystal', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1000, 'A greater crystal, diamond shaped, that holds a LIFE ESSENCE - a character''s awareness, intelligence, emotions and personality - preserved for centuries. Only one life force fits in a gem. Transferral needs a living person and 25 minutes of ritual for an unwilling subject rendered unconscious, or about 15 minutes of concentration for a willing one (five for a mage who has done it before). 1000 M.D.C., regenerating up to 200 points every 12 hours; if the crystal is destroyed the character inside it DIES. Inside, the essence has no awareness of space or time unless grounded. Someone physically holding the crystal can be psionically linked to it: the essence sees and hears everything they do, and can talk to them, but cannot feel, smell, taste, read thoughts, use psionics, cast spells, possess them or impart skills - and the link breaks instantly if the crystal is put in a pocket or set down. The other route is a new body: the crystal is embedded in the forehead of a golem, zombie, worm zombie, mummy, robot, mindless clone or cyborg, and all five senses engage. Mental attributes, skills, O.C.C., memories, psionics and I.S.P. are unchanged; physical attributes and M.D.C. are entirely those of the new body. P.P.E. is 4D6 in an inorganic or dead body and 2D4x10 in a living one. Without a body the character cannot use or improve skills or gain experience.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.112-113'),
  ('the-eye-of-wormwood', 'The Eye of Wormwood', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A RARE greater crystal - a sparkling golden yellow gem that gives its owner the power to cast prayers of communion with Wormwood, like a priest or wormspeaker. It offers eight spells per 24 hours in any combination or repetition, drawn from Close an Opening, Create a Fountain of Water, Create an Opening, Create Stairs, Hell Fire, Locate Places of Evil, Locate Food & Resources and Locate Home Town. Duration and spell strength are equal to a 6th level wormspeaker.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.113'),
  ('the-heart-of-wormwood', 'The Heart of Wormwood', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A RARE greater crystal - a large, sparkling golden yellow gem, the Eye''s bigger counterpart, giving its owner the power to cast prayers of communion with Wormwood. It offers eight spells per 24 hours in any combination or repetition, drawn from Control Temperature, Create Shelter, Destroy Life Force Cauldron, Heat Point, Hell Fire, Invisible to Magic Seeing, Life Fuel, Locate Places of Evil and Summon Edible Grubs. Duration and spell strength are equal to a 6th level wormspeaker.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.113'),
  ('magic-booster-crystal', 'Magic Booster Crystal', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A greater crystal - a sparkling, many-faceted light blue crystal. Powers: doubles the duration and range of magic spells, and increases the character''s P.P.E. and P.E. by 25%. Duration: the doubling is always on and happens automatically whenever a spell is cast, provided the crystal is held or worn.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.113'),
  ('spell-gem-of-destruction', 'Spell Gem of Destruction', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A greater crystal - a deep blue, almost black, diamond-like gem. It offers its owner a total of eight spells per 24 hours in any combination or repetition, drawn from Fuel Flame, Fire Bolt, Fire Ball, Circle of Flame, Call Lightning, Life Drain, Negate Magic and Paralysis: Lesser. Duration and spell strength are equal to a 6th level wizard.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.113-114'),
  ('spell-gem-of-dimensions', 'Spell Gem of Dimensions', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A greater crystal - a crystal blue gem whose magic alters space and time. It offers eight spells and the P.P.E. to work them at no cost to the user, cast per 24 hours in any combination or repetition, drawn from Invisibility (self), Close Rift, Dimensional Portal/Rift, Time Slip, Time Hole, Teleport: Lesser, Teleport: Superior and Mystic Portal. Duration and spell strength are equal to a 6th level wizard.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.113'),
  ('spell-gem-of-illusion', 'Spell Gem of Illusion', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A greater crystal - a green crystal of illusion magic. It offers eight spells and the P.P.E. to work them at no cost to the user, cast per 24 hours in any combination or repetition, drawn from Apparition, Concealment, Fool''s Gold, Hallucination, Horrific Illusion, Mask of Deceit, Multiple Image and Wisps of Confusion. Duration and spell strength are equal to a 6th level wizard.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.113-114'),
  ('spell-gem-of-magic', 'Spell Gem of Magic', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A greater crystal - a white crystal with a deep blue diamond at its core, for spells of mystical significance. It offers eight spells and the P.P.E. to work them at no cost to the user, cast per 24 hours in any combination or repetition, drawn from Anti-Magic Cloud, Dispel Magic Barriers, Eyes of Thoth, Magic Pigeon, Metamorphosis: Mist, Negate Magic, Tongues and Sense Magic. Duration and spell strength are equal to a 6th level wizard.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.113-114'),
  ('spell-gem-of-protection', 'Spell Gem of Protection', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A greater crystal - an amber crystal of mystic protection. It offers eight spells and the P.P.E. to work them at no cost to the user, cast per 24 hours in any combination or repetition, drawn from Armor of Ithan, Escape, Impervious to Energy, Impervious to Fire, Impervious to Poison, Negate Magic, Repel Animals and Sanctum. Duration and spell strength are equal to a 6th level wizard.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.114'),
  ('lesser-energy-cell-crystal', 'Lesser Energy Cell Crystal', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A lesser crystal, usually pure white like a diamond, holding mystic energy that priests, practitioners of magic and techno-wizard devices can draw on. It regenerates half its P.P.E. in 12 hours and all of it in 24. Capacity by size: robin to chicken egg 10 P.P.E., baseball 25 P.P.E., grapefruit 50 P.P.E.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.111-112'),
  ('lesser-spell-gem', 'Lesser Spell Gem', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A smaller, less powerful spell gem, usually white or green. It offers its owner two spells and the P.P.E. to work them at no cost to the user, chosen from any of the first and second level spells in the Rifts RPG (pp.166-167). The selection is typically random, made by the G.M., and once selected the spells cannot be changed. Two spells can be cast per 24 hours - two different ones or the same one twice. Duration and spell strength are equal to a 2nd level wizard.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.114'),
  ('light-crystal', 'Light Crystal', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A lesser crystal - a light yellow crystal with a lot of sparkle. It can cast each of Blinding Flash, Globe of Daylight and Ignite Fire twice per 24 hours at no P.P.E. cost to the user. Duration and spell strength are equal to a 2nd level wizard.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.114'),
  ('finder-crystal', 'Finder Crystal', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A lesser crystal - a small, sparkling golden yellow crystal, and one of the few magic gems carrying prayers of communion with Wormwood. It can cast each of Locate Places of Evil, Locate Food & Resources, Locate Home Town and Create an Opening twice per 24 hours at no P.P.E. cost to the user. Duration and spell strength are equal to a 2nd level wizard.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.114'),
  ('shadow-crystal', 'Shadow Crystal', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A lesser crystal - a dusky blue-grey crystal with a little sparkle. It can cast each of Chameleon, Invisibility and Shadow Meld twice per 24 hours at no P.P.E. cost to the user. Duration and spell strength are equal to a 2nd level wizard.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.114'),
  ('spell-gem-blank', 'Spell Gem Blank', 'rifts', 'magic', NULL, NULL, 'No published price. Wormwood runs on barter and these are grown by the living planet, not sold; the Priest of Light O.C.C. states Money: Not applicable (p.54).', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A lesser crystal - a pure, clear crystal like a lesser spell gem, only BLANK and waiting for two spells to be placed in it. The character who finds it gives it its magic: a practitioner of magic casts a spell at the crystal, the gem absorbs it and is encoded with that power. Because of that, the strength of the spell equals that of the spell caster who gave it, and the spells may come from the Rifts RPG, temporal magic, elemental magic or communion with Wormwood magic. Each spell can be cast twice per 24 hours. Two spells total, and once placed they cannot be changed.', 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood p.114')
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO UPDATE SET
       name = excluded.name,
       system = excluded.system,
       category = excluded.category,
       weight_lbs = excluded.weight_lbs,
       cost = excluded.cost,
       cost_note = excluded.cost_note,
       damage = excluded.damage,
       is_mega_damage = excluded.is_mega_damage,
       range = excluded.range,
       payload = excluded.payload,
       rate_of_fire = excluded.rate_of_fire,
       ar = excluded.ar,
       sdc = excluded.sdc,
       mdc = excluded.mdc,
       description = excluded.description,
       source_book = excluded.source_book;

-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code.
SELECT count(*) AS wormwood_gear FROM gear WHERE source_book LIKE 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood%';
SELECT category, count(*) AS n FROM gear WHERE source_book LIKE 'Rifts Dimension Book 1: Wormwood%' GROUP BY category ORDER BY category;
SELECT count(*) AS total_gear FROM gear;

-- Records this run. One row per run rather than per file: every statement
-- above guards itself, so this script is safe to re-run.
-- See db/migrations/024-data-script-runs.sql.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-wormwood-gear.sql');
